  "id": "093d4938-c9ba-4147-b0a3-6f6711ed1c47",
  "title": "FDA warns of potential vision loss risk from GLP-1 drugs",
  "summary": "The FDA has found evidence of a potential increased risk of a rare eye condition linked to GLP-1 medications, including Ozempic, Zepbound, and Wegovy. The risk appears small and data is mixed, but FDA wants patients to be aware.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Several medical studies found that GLP-1 medications may increase the risk of nonarteritic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy (NAION).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "FDA has stated that the risk appears small and data is mixed, but they are urging patients to be cautious.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "GLP-1 drugs used for weight management and diabetes have been linked to potential vision loss.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
